`crimes context` confirms the three findings and reports no related files or likely tests. I’d refactor `Card` into a non-interactive layout with an explicit action:

```tsx
export function Card({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <article className="card">
      <div className="card__content">{children}</div>
      <aside className="card__sidebar">sidebar</aside>
      <button type="button" className="card__action" onClick={handleOpen}>
        Open details
      </button>
    </article>
  );
}
```

Tie the changes to each finding:

- `accessible_interaction_risk`: remove `onClick` from the outer `<div>` and use a native `<button>` with meaningful visible text. This supplies keyboard behavior, focusability, and button semantics automatically. Making the whole card a button would be risky because arbitrary `children` could contain nested interactive elements.
- `design_token_escape`: move presentation out of JSX and replace all raw colors, spacing, shadow, sizing, and focus values with named Tailwind/design-system tokens. Existing `brand`, `surface`, and `ink` tokens can cover the focus ring, background, and text; add intentional `border`, `muted`, `cardShadow`, and sizing tokens rather than inventing more literals inside the component.
- `responsive_fragility`: replace `width: 800`, `width: 720`, `height: 600`, and the fixed sidebar width with a fluid container: `inline-size: 100%`, a tokenized `max-inline-size`, automatic height, and a grid using `minmax(0, 1fr)`. Use a container query to stack the sidebar below the content when space is constrained. Replace `fontSize: 18` with the typography scale or a token-backed `clamp()`.

Conceptually, the extracted styles should follow this shape:

```css
.card {
  container-type: inline-size;
  inline-size: 100%;
  max-inline-size: var(--size-card-max);
  padding: var(--space-6);
  color: var(--color-ink);
  background: var(--color-surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) var(--size-sidebar);
}

.card__content {
  min-inline-size: 0;
  font-size: var(--font-body-lg);
}

@container (inline-size < 40rem) {
  .card {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
```

